> **Why do standard panel regressions using local weather shocks have limited external validity for climate change?**  
> A. They typically identify immediate local responses but not effects transmitted through trade or migration.  
> B. They often have difficulty distinguishing temperature effects from other changing local conditions.  
> C. They use temporary, localized, and potentially unanticipated variation to infer effects of persistent, global, anticipated climate change.  
