> **What is a key limitation of cross-sectional climate-impact studies?**  
> A. They may mistake differences in current climate for effects of expected future climate.  
> B. They may miss economic spillovers because they treat each location’s climate as changing independently.  
> C. They may attribute climate-related differences to climate when locations also differ in institutions, development, geography, and other unobserved factors.  
